{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","reason":"Hosts js_safe_result() + install_js_safe_guard() on the existing mcp.tool-rebinding seam, reaching both the content and structuredContent branches."},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"Wires install_js_safe_guard(mcp) after install_error_guard(mcp), before the tool registrars."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"Sibling fix: 3 declared signed_at annotations widened int -> int|str so model_validate stops coercing the JS-safe string back to a bare out-of-range integer in structuredContent."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json","reason":"created_at / last_reopened_at / source_created_at accept the decimal-string wire form (all optional keys), and updated_at is now DECLARED here instead of riding through as an undeclared additional property."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json","reason":"signed_at accepts the decimal-string wire form (REQUIRED key - flagged for operator review against docs/api-stability.md:23); its top-level description no longer contradicts the property by calling signed_at a ns-epoch integer."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json","reason":"signed_at accepts the decimal-string wire form (REQUIRED key - flagged for operator review)."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":"signed_at accepts the decimal-string wire form (REQUIRED key - flagged for operator review); this is the schema whose declared-int coercion made structuredContent disagree with the content block."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json","reason":"The shared comment object is the other carrier of raw ns timestamps: comment.timestamp and comment.source_created_at are documented with the decimal-string wire form and the BigInt/int() consuming rule, so the retype is described where the shared definition lives rather than only in the per-tool schemas that $ref it."},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"Regenerated by python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types; verified byte-identical to generator output (no hand-edit drift)."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py","reason":"New RED-first regression test (5 cases): drives the real MCP server on the direct call_tool path and the registered CallToolRequest handler, asserts no integer outside the RFC 8259 range reaches either response branch, asserts lossless round-trip, and adds a structural guard failing CI if a new ns-timestamp field is declared as bare int."},{"path":"docs/output-schemas.md","reason":"The consumer-facing mirror of the schema change: documents that an out-of-range ns timestamp goes on the MCP wire as an exact decimal string and must be parsed with int()/BigInt(), never Number(), so readers of the schema contract are not left to infer the rule from individual property descriptions."},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"The --output json stability row said required keys are not retyped, which this change breaks for signed_at. The row is amended to state that a pre-1.0 break is permitted but is never a silent exception - it must be recorded as BREAKING in the release notes and CHANGELOG - so the policy and the shipped behaviour agree."},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"Records the retype as an explicit BREAKING (pre-1.0) entry naming the keys, the surfaces and the consumer action, which is the disclosure the amended api-stability rule now requires."},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"Same BREAKING disclosure under [Unreleased]; the version itself is deliberately not bumped here because this repo bumps pyproject in a dedicated release commit under a lockstep guard against server.json."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","reason":"Prose correction found by the repo-wide sweep: the skill told agents created_at is an integer, which is now false on the MCP surface. It states both wire forms and tells the agent to coerce with int() rather than assume either, so the packaged guidance does not contradict the schema."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787890028597464706,"uuid":"3bbc32b7-8b80-4d53-9eec-9206fb11390b"}